---
source: tests/cli/tools.rs
info:
  program: slcr
  args:
    - tools
    - update
    - "--help"
  env:
    HOME: "[HOME]"
    XDG_DATA_HOME: "[DATA_HOME]"
---
success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Re-fetch a declared tool's descriptor from its source, check it, re-pin it, and install it

Usage: slcr tools update [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>
          The name the tool is declared under in SLCR.toml

Options:
      --enable-colors <ENABLE_COLORS>
          Whether to color the output

          Possible values:
          - always: Always color the output
          - never:  Never color the output
          - auto:   Detect whether the terminal is a tty before deciding to color
          
          [default: auto]

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Sets the maximum log level. Defaults to INFO. Options are 'trace', 'debug', 'info', 'warn', 'error', and 'off'. 'off' implies no logger will occur. Options are case-insensitive
          
          [env: LOG_LEVEL=]
          [default: info]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

----- stderr -----
